## Self-checks (operator confirms each before running the scan)

- [ ] **a. Burner aged ≥ 7 days in this guild.** Burner account joined the
      target guild at least seven days ago. Fresh-join + immediate scrape is
      a classic self-bot pattern; a quiet warm-up window flattens the curve.
- [ ] **b. Burner has done normal browsing today.** Open Discord in the burner's
      regular browser profile, click around in 2-3 channels, react to nothing.
      The gateway PRESENCE UPDATE we send needs to land on a session that
      Discord has already seen behaving like a human today.
- [ ] **c. FileVault on (macOS) / BitLocker on (Windows) / LUKS on (Linux).**
      `state/` and `output/` carry burner cookies and third-party PII; at-rest
      encryption is non-negotiable per security-model.md §6 and the operator
      obligations in `docs/claude/development.md`.
- [ ] **d. No captcha event today on this burner.** Not in the scanner, not in
      the browser. If you got a captcha when logging into Discord this morning,
      stop here and follow Runbook 3 (24-72h cool-down) before scanning.
- [ ] **e. Target guild is low-stakes.** Not medical / mental-health / minors-
      focused / addiction-recovery / no-archive-rule. (Re-read the prohibited
      classes in `docs/claude/development.md` if in doubt.)

## CLI smoke (no Discord traffic)

- [ ] `discord-scanner version` exits 0 and prints a version string.
- [ ] `discord-scanner store-token` round-trips. Verify with:
      `keyring get discord-scanner burner-1` returns a non-empty value.
      (The token is masked in scanner logs but exposed in raw form by the
      `keyring` CLI — close the terminal scrollback after.)
- [ ] `cp config.live.yaml.example config.live.yaml` and edit
      `discovery.manual_invites[0]` to the real invite code.
- [ ] `discord-scanner scan --config config.live.yaml --guild <GUILD_ID> --dry-run`
      exits 0. Verify the printed plan reads the right guild filter and shows
      `max_messages_per_scan = 200`.

## Hard-stop signals (abort the scan if you see any of these)

- `captcha_aborted` — exit code 2; follow Runbook 3 (`docs/claude/development.md`).
  Do NOT retry.
- 401 on `/users/@me/guilds` (visible in `discord-scanner list-guilds`,
  also surfaces in scan logs) — token is dead; follow Runbook 2 (token
  compromise / rotation).
- Repeated `gateway_invalid_session` events (more than 2 in a single scan) —
  fingerprint divergence likely; abort, file a `decisions.md` note, and do
  NOT rotate the burner blindly without first checking the gateway/REST
  fingerprint parity (single-source-of-truth: `HttpSettings.fingerprint()`).

